# Template for /etc/us-stock-helper/opend.env — copy it there, then set the
# real value. The deployed file is owned by root and mode 0600; systemd reads
# it as the manager, so the service account never needs access to it.
#
# Everything in OPEND_ARGS ends up on the command line, and command lines are
# world-readable through /proc. An account, a password, a password hash or a
# trade-unlock code here is disclosed to every process on the host. Put login
# material only in the OpenD configuration file, which the operator writes by
# hand, and confirm the flag your OpenD build accepts with `./OpenD --help`.
OPEND_ARGS=-cfg_file=/etc/us-stock-helper/opend.conf
